  ],
  "blocks": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Providence Mount St Vincent in Seattle, or the Mount, is no ordinary nursing home. It has its own preschool and welcomes "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b1",
      "number": 1
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " five days a week. Therefore, its elderly residents are often in the same room with young people. The Mount hopes that this will make the elderly feel less "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b2",
      "number": 2
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " and that they are here “to live, not to die”. The challenges are many, but worth the effort."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "While it’s not common to combine preschools with nursing homes, the Mount isn’t the only "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b3",
      "number": 3
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ". A Japanese man, Shimada Masaharu, once did it in Tokyo in 1976. By 1998, the city had sixteen such centres. It was around this time that the idea "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b4",
      "number": 4
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " to North America. Since then, more centres have sprung up on both sides of the Pacific."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Studies show that making friends with young people is good for the "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b5",
      "number": 5
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ". It makes them healthier and happier. They also smile and talk more with people of their age. Children can "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b6",
      "number": 6
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " the interactions, too. Among other things, they learn how to "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b7",
      "number": 7
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " the elderly or people with "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "disabilities",
      "ref": "v-disability"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "At the Mount, there are many "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b8",
      "number": 8
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " for older people to interact with children. They are welcome in the classrooms and can organise activities for the children. They can also take part in some of the activities. If a local musician comes around to perform, they sing and dance together with the children."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "This "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "injection",
      "ref": "v-injection"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " of life has worked wonders. One lady had advanced Alzheimer’s and was unable to "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b9",
      "number": 9
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " clearly. But after she was wheeled into the baby room, she could suddenly say full sentences. Part of her brain became "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b10",
      "number": 10
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " again thanks to the smiling young faces around her. It’s a touching story, one of many to be told at the Mount."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
